 "nl": [
  "Hosts in nvr may reach backup over RDP (TCP 3389) and syslog (UDP 514).",
  "student-lab may use any TCP port towards partners, except FTP (TCP 21), SMB (TCP 445), RDP (TCP 3389), which must be blocked.",
  "Allow partners to connect to backup using LDAP (TCP 389) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "backup is isolated: it may only reach finance on HTTPS (TCP 443); finance on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Deny all traffic from nvr to dmz-web (this overrides any public service).",
  "Restrict vpn-users so that its only permitted destinations are finance on DNS over UDP 53; partners on NTP (UDP 123); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Hosts in backup may reach mail over PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and DNS over UDP 53 and MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "backup must accept RTSP (TCP 554) and HTTP (TCP 80) from mail.",
  "Hosts in dns-servers may reach partners over HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "Block SMB (TCP 445), FTP (TCP 21), RDP (TCP 3389) from backup to dns-servers; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "mail must accept IMAP (TCP 143) and RTSP (TCP 554) from dmz-web.",
  "dev-lab must accept LDAP (TCP 389) from mail.",
  "Make HTTPS (TCP 443) and NTP (UDP 123) on vpn-users reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Make HTTPS (TCP 443) on student-lab reachable from all internal zones.",
  "finance must accept DNS over UDP 53 and HTTPS (TCP 443) from mail.",
  "Apart from mail on syslog (UDP 514); student-lab on HTTPS (TCP 443), all traffic originating in dmz-web must be dropped.",
  "Apart from dev-lab on HTTPS (TCP 443); partners on HTTPS (TCP 443), all traffic originating in student-lab must be dropped.",
  "vpn-users must never reach dns-servers, regardless of any other rule.",
  "backup offers HTTP (TCP 80) and NTP (UDP 123) to every zone.",
  "finance must accept HTTP (TCP 80) and SSH (TCP 22) from vpn-users.",
  "dev-lab must accept NTP (UDP 123) from finance.",
  "Hosts in dmz-web may reach student-lab over RDP (TCP 3389) and SNMP (UDP 161).",
  "Hosts in vpn-users may reach mail over HTTPS (TCP 443) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Hosts in student-lab may reach finance over RDP (TCP 3389) and LDAP (TCP 389).",
  "Hosts in nvr may reach dns-servers over syslog (UDP 514) and RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Block TFTP (UDP 69) from vpn-users to partners; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "Hosts in finance may reach dmz-web over HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "dev-lab must never reach mail, regardless of any other rule.",
  "dmz-web may use any UDP port towards mail, except TFTP (UDP 69), which must be blocked.",
  "Deny all traffic from nvr to backup (this overrides any public service).",
  "dmz-web may use TCP ports 1024-65535 towards student-lab, except MySQL (TCP 3306), PostgreSQL (TCP 5432), which must be blocked."
 ],
